Reason: tile_layer_find(depth, x, y) walked every tile of the room backwards for each call. Speed blocks look up their
tile with it as they break: in rm_a6b02 a speed run made 126 calls in one frame, ~15 µs each on the console (1.9 ms).
The tile-skip grid (patches 0078 and 0080) already holds every live tile of a depth in the cells its box covers (or
among the always visited), so the call now tests only the tiles in the point's cell and keeps the one with the highest
array index, the one the backwards walk found first. A deleted tile's pseudo index is among the deleted ones, and a
live one's array index is its pseudo index less the deleted ones below it. When the grid or the tile run isn't current,
the walk runs as before.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

